From 239b11e0a72f76af59156773310bf23eda966f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:43:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): metadata-only ask amendments no longer re-send a
 blocked notice [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`hermes kanban block <id> ... --human-request <json> --metadata-only` records
a `blocked` event with `metadata_only: true` on a card that is already
parked. Both notice paths (gateway notifier `_fmt_blocked` and the TUI/Desktop
`_format_kanban_event_text`) rendered it as a fresh "⏸ ... blocked — actor"
notice, including to the chat that made the edit, so the user saw a new block
and a repeated ask (t_01a1ce412fbf6e7f).

- The subscriber chat that is the event's actor gets nothing: no ping and no
  wake; the claimed cursor still passes the event. The actor label carries the
  gateway DM session key `agent:<ns>:<platform>:dm:<id>` or the raw session id,
  and the subscription stores the bare `<id>`; `actor_is_chat` matches both and
  never reduces group/thread keys.
- Other subscribers get one line: "ask updated (card still blocked): <new
  action> — open task: <link>", no "blocked —" notice. A card no longer
  parked at delivery reports its current state, as block_notice does.
- Real block transitions are unchanged, including to the actor's own chat.

Tests: notifier end-to-end through the real metadata-only writer
(classify_parked_request) for (a) silent + cursor passed, (b) ask-updated
line, (c) real block unchanged; renderer tests on both entry paths and the
(d) id-matching table in test_actionable_block_notices.
